#: includes/core/class-mxchat-plus-admin.php:143
msgid "Enabled"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:23
msgid ""
"Turns the DuckDB / MotherDuck vector store on. MxChat uses it only for the "
"bots routed below: the default bot with Default-bot routing, other bots with "
"Multi-Bot routing. Every other bot keeps its own Pinecone or WordPress-"
"database storage. When disabled, MxChat falls back to its default behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:30
msgid "Backend"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:34
msgid "MotherDuck (cloud, via ATTACH)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:38
msgid "DuckDB embedded (local file)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:43
msgid "Default-bot routing"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:49
msgid "Route default-bot Pinecone calls through this plugin (Option B reach)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:53
msgid ""
"MxChat reads the default bot's Pinecone settings straight from the database, "
"so the filter this plugin uses for other bots never reaches it. Enable this "
"to answer that read with the DuckDB proxy, so the default bot is served by "
"DuckDB too. Your stored Pinecone settings are kept: switching this off gives "
"them back to MxChat. Leave OFF if the default bot should keep real Pinecone "
"or the WordPress database, or if you've applied the upstream patch (Option "
"A) — the patch path doesn't need this setting."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:60
msgid "Multi-Bot routing"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:66
msgid "Route every Multi-Bot bot through this plugin"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:69
msgid "Or only these bot IDs (comma-separated):"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:76
msgid ""
"For MxChat's Multi-Bot add-on. A routed bot reads and writes its own DuckDB "
"namespace, named after its bot ID, instead of the storage the add-on gives "
"it — so it no longer sees the knowledge MxChat keeps in the WordPress "
"database, which all bots share. A bot on a Pinecone document index is never "
"routed. Bots that are not routed keep their own settings."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:91
msgid ""
"This install predates the setting and still routes every bot, because DuckDB "
"could not be read to find which bots have vectors there. As soon as it "
"answers, only those bots stay routed. Saving this page without changing "
"these fields leaves that upgrade pending; untick the box or list bot IDs to "
"choose now."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:100
msgid "Keep routing every bot (skip the automatic upgrade)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-activation.php:106
msgid "The Multi-Bot add-on is not active, so this setting has no effect."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-bot-overrides.php:24
msgid "Per-bot retrieval overrides"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/duckdb/partials/section-bot-overrides.php:27
msgid ""
"Tune retrieval per bot for multi-bot installs. Only hybrid search, dedup, "
"the query cache, and the slow-query threshold can vary per bot — backend and "
"storage are always shared. A bot with \"Override\" off inherits the global "
"Retrieval settings above. You can also set these from code with the "
"mxchat_plus_duckdb_bot_config filter."
msgstr ""

