#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:25
#: includes/core/class-mxchat-plus-admin.php:72
msgid "Click tracking"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:29
msgid ""
"Sends an analytics event when a visitor clicks a link inside a chatbot "
"answer, or a suggested question. Nothing leaves the page until one of the "
"two destinations below is switched on."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:43
msgid "Destinations"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:48
msgid "Send events to Matomo"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:52
msgid ""
"Events go through the Matomo tracker already loaded on the page, so the site "
"id is the one in your existing Matomo snippet — there is nothing to enter "
"here. On a page with no Matomo snippet, nothing is sent."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:60
msgid "Send events to Google Analytics 4"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:64
msgid ""
"Requires gtag() to be loaded by something else — a GA4 plugin, a tag "
"manager, or the snippet in your theme. This module never injects the GA4 tag "
"itself, and sends nothing when gtag() is absent."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:72
msgid "Chat opened"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:77
msgid "Also send an event when a visitor opens the chat window"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: Matomo event action, keep as is; 2: GA4 event name, keep as is
#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:85
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Off by default. Adds the Matomo action %1$s and the GA4 event %2$s, at most "
"once per chatbot per page load. A chatbot embedded in the page is never "
"reported: it is on screen from the start, so nobody opened it. A floating "
"window counts however it was revealed, including by another plugin or a "
"theme button. Needs MxChat 3.2.22 or later; older versions send nothing."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:95
msgid "Session id"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:100
msgid "Include the MxChat session id in each event"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:104
msgid ""
"The session id is the join key into MxChat's transcripts table: with it, a "
"click can be traced back to the conversation that produced it. It also means "
"the id leaves the site — analytics vendors sit outside MxChat's own erasure "
"path, so a deletion handled by MxChat does not reach them. Turning this off "
"is the conservative choice; the events still work without it."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:113
msgid "Matomo custom dimension"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:122
msgid ""
"The session id is also written to this Matomo custom dimension — give the id "
"(1 to 999) of the dimension you created in Matomo. Leave it at 0 to send no "
"custom dimension; it has no effect while the session id is not sent."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:130
msgid "Debug"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:135
msgid "Log every event to the browser console"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:139
msgid ""
"Each event is printed in the DevTools console, prefixed [MxChat Plus "
"tracking]. It logs for every visitor, not only for administrators, so this "
"is meant to be switched back off once you have checked that the events look "
"right."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:152
msgid "Clicked links"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:158
msgid ""
"MxChat logs link clicks server-side into its own table, which it creates "
"when the plugin is activated and again after each MxChat update. That table "
"does not exist on this site, so there is nothing to report. Deactivating and "
"reactivating MxChat creates it now."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:167
msgid ""
"This report counts what MxChat itself records server-side, which is a "
"narrower population than the events sent above: MxChat only tracks absolute "
"http(s) links inside answers — never relative links, and never suggested "
"questions. The two figures measure different things and will not match, by "
"construction."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:174
msgid ""
"Counts are not comparable across the MxChat 3.2.24 and 3.2.25 updates, in "
"either direction: MxChat changed which clicks it logs and which addresses it "
"turns into links, so one page can also appear under two spellings. Compare "
"the Sessions column rather than Clicks across those dates."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:181
msgid "No click has been recorded yet."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of clicks, 2: number of distinct links, 3: number of distinct sessions
#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:189
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s clicks recorded, on %2$s links, across %3$s sessions."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: number of links listed in the table
#: admin/views/tracking/settings.php:200
#, php-format
msgid "Only the %s most clicked links are listed here."
msgstr ""

